40
]. Following an absorption event, the ejected photoelectron wave may be scattered by electrons in atoms surrounding the absorbing atom, creating quantum interference, which can be conceptualized as arising from constructive and destructive interference between outgoing and backscattered de Broglie photoelectron waves [
44
