B
= 81.4°) in Johann geometry on a 1 m Rowland circle [
155
]. Conventional Zn K-edge XAS spectra were collected on beamline 7-3 using a Si(220) double-crystal monochromator with harmonic rejection accomplished by detuning the monochromator to 60% of the peak intensity. X-ray absorption was measured simultaneously with the Zn Kα
1
fluorescence excitation spectrum, using an array of 30 discrete Ge detectors [
155
]. For both beamlines, the incident X-ray energy was calibrated to the first inflection point of a Zn metal foil (9660.7 eV). Samples were maintained at 10 K and inclined at 45° to the incident X-ray beam to give a path length of 2.8 mm [
155
].
